+# Pickup reminders
+
+For volunteers considering changes to pickup reminders, including switching to email to save the SMS cost. Pickup
+reminders use SMS because the email trial left more pantry orders uncollected and fresh food went to waste. This
+page records the outcome after volunteers repeatedly proposed the same switch.
+
+## Why SMS
+
+During the April–June 2025 email trial, the provider reported that 34% of reminder emails were never opened. Missed
+pickups rose from 6% to 13% of pantry orders. Each missed pickup left a packed bag whose fresh food went in the bin
+at closing time. Many members share a family phone and do not check email, but see SMS messages.
+
+SMS reminders resumed on July 1, 2025, and missed pickups were back to 6% by August. Email was proposed again to
+save the reported €40 monthly SMS cost, but the maintainer kept SMS: reaching members and avoiding wasted food
+outweighed that saving. The trial results and the decision are recorded in [issue 52](../../notes/issue-52.md).
+
+## Implementation
+
+The reminder timing, message and channel selection live in [the reminder code](../../larder/reminders.py).
